WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.000
-It's nice to see you.
Thanks for coming in person.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.367
-Jimmy, listen, this is a wee
gift from my son Daniel, who --

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:09.534
He and his business partner
started this tequila business

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:12.100
that's winning international
gold medals.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.234
-I mean, yeah.

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:16.968
Take care, everybody.
Thank you. Bye-bye.

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.901
I say gracias. De Nada.

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:25.100
I know your son --
your other son is an actor.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.267
-Michael. Yes, he is.
-Michael.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.567
-Yeah.
-Is he enjoying it?

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:32.634
-You know, he's in the world
where, you know, I've told him

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:35.501
70% of actors are out of work
all the time.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:39.434
This is true. I said,
"Welcome to the club, buddy."

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:41.601
-Yeah.
-But he's doing okay.

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.868
He's got a good presence.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:46.200
Well, I mean, coming from
you guys --

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.367
-But from his mother's side,
God rest her,

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:51.968
his mother's side of the family,
they go back

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:55.567
theatrically to the late 1700s.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:56.901
-Wow. Is that right? Geez.

00:00:56.901 --> 00:01:00.100
-So when he says it's in
his blood, it's in his blood.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.367
-It's actually in his blood,
yeah, yeah.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.868
I heard a rumor about you, I was
reading online -- a good one.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:08.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.100
That you may be doing a reboot
of "The Naked Gun."

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.934
-Yes, hopefully.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:15.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.834
-With Seth McFarlane.
Is he involved?

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:21.200
-Seth McFarlane is writing it
with his team.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.067
He may direct it.

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:29.601
He was approached by Paramount
Studios, and they picked me.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:30.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.634
-How fun would that be?

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.067
I would be there tomorrow.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:36.734
-Jimmy, it's either going to be
the end of my career or --

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:39.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.300
-You know, we had
Brian Tyree Henry on the show.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.467
And we were talking about you.
-Yes. He's a great actor.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.501
-A talented guy, he's funny.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:49.501
We were talking about --
He did a film with you.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:50.634
We had a picture of you guys --

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:53.100
-The one film I was
totally miscast in.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.133
-Oh, is that right?
-Totally miscast in this film.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:56.300
-Why do you think
you were miscast?

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.434
-Because I saw it.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:02:01.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:05.033
You know, I made -- Up to
Christmas, I made 100 films.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.634
I saw "Widows" --

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.601
this is the film with
Brian and myself in it.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.167
Brian's terrific in it.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:13.501
And I was almost in tears
I was so bad.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:14.901
I was so miscast in that film.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.334
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:17.901
-But you're never bad
in anything.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.234
-I was bad in this.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:21.334
[ Laughter ]
-Wow. Alright.

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:24.634
I was talking about your red
carpet you did before this film,

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:28.033
which made me laugh because I
go, "Liam's a great guy.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.901
I mean, he's funny and he
doesn't take it too serious."

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:32.767
He goes, "Yeah," he goes, "What
were you doing here?"

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:36.567
And he goes, "We're were doing
Blue Steel."

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:37.801
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.634
-And I go,
"Wait, from 'Zoolander?'"

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.133
He's like, "Yeah.
We're taking photos

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.767
and Liam leans over and goes,
'Give him Blue Steel.'"

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:46.033
And I just thought it was
the funniest thing.

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.300
-Yeah, we all did.
-Do you always do Blue Steel?

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.968
-All the time. All the time.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:51.501
Yeah.
-Are you a "Zoolander" fan?

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.400
-I loved "Zoolander."
-Me too.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.767
-I loved it.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.834
-I was doing a film with
Chris Hemsworth

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.100
two or three years ago.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.434
-Three years ago.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.901
And we had to pose for a couple
of photographs,

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:05.234
and I said my usual line.

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:06.534
I said, "Okay, they got that.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.133
Let's do a Blue Steel."

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.634
And Chris went,
"I'm going to do a Magnum."

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:13.667
And I went, "Oh, okay."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:15.367
-That's funny.
That's very funny.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.100
-So he was totally in on it.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.133
-Yeah, because Magnum is
the same as Blue Steel.

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:21.100
-Pretty much.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.767
There's a very slight
difference.

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:23.868
-There's a slight difference.

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.000
Can you show everyone
the Blue Steel?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.234
Could we give each other --
-Yeah, okay.

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:28.300
How far are you?
-Yeah, right here.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.934
That, right there.
-Okay.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.701
-Here we go. Blue Steel.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.634
Oh, my God.

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:42.100
Right now Ben Stiller
is freaking out

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.868
'cause that is the best thing
I've ever seen.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.400
-Do you want to see the Magnum?

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.834
-Let's see the Magnum,
yeah, yeah.

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.400
Drum roll, can we get --

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:55.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.901
-You see the difference?
-Yeah, I did.

00:03:57.901 --> 00:03:59.934
Yeah, yeah,
I saw the difference.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:03.167
I want to talk about
your new movie "Blacklight."

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:07.434
When you've been on the show,
I remember "Taken," when it --

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:11.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:14.133
When that movie came out, you
were like, "Yeah, I don't know.

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:17.734
I was always -- I'll try
this action film thing."

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.501
You talked to Luc Besson.
You chased him down?

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:23.000
-Yeah. My wife was in --
They were showing her film

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.901
at the Shanghai Film Festival
and Luc was there.

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.167
Luc Besson. A wonderful man.
-Yeah.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.968
-Terrific director, innovator.
-Yeah.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:32.501
-Anyway, he was head
of the jury.

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:35.367
And I had read this "Taken"
script and I thought,

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.067
"Well, it's going
straight to video,

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.968
but it's a cool --
it's a cool little story."

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:41.901
-It's a cool little story,
but it'll go straight to video?

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.534
-And it'll go straight to video,
and no one will see it,

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:47.567
but I get to fight a lot,
which I wanted to do.

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:49.901
So I met Luc and I said, "Luc,
I'm sure I'm not

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:53.367
on your list at all,
but I used to box as a kid

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:55.501
and I did sword fights
in a few movies,"

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.868
and I said, "I'd love the chance
to do this."

00:04:57.868 --> 00:05:00.868
So push came to shove
and I got the part.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:03.334
-Yeah.
-It was three months in Paris

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:06.901
working out with these stunt
guys five days a week.

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:09.501
It was terrific. I was like
a kid in a candy store.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:11.300
And then I thought,
"Right, that's over.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.467
It's going straight to video."

00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:16.801
And my wife, God rest her,
when the film came out --

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:19.767
She always brought me a cup of
tea and a bran muffin

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:22.100
every morning
when I was at home.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.400
So Sunday I hear her
coming up the stairs

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.801
with her tray,
giggling, laughing.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.334
Something's up.

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.634
So she gives me the tea and the
bran muffin and she's giggling.

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:32.601
I said, "What's wrong?"

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:36.033
She said, "You won't believe it.
'Taken' is number --"

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.067
I think it was number two.

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.067
It came in number two
over the weekend.

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:42.334
Then the following week
it came in number three.

00:05:42.334 --> 00:05:44.434
Then it moved up to
number two again,

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:45.968
and it hovered around there.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.634
So it became a hit.

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:49.200
-Yeah, you think? Yeah.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:53.300
She was laughing. She was like,

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.968
"This movie you thought was
going to go straight to video."

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.634
-And not because of -- You know,
the writing was wonderful

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:02.734
and Pierre Morel, the director,
directed incredibly well.

00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:06.467
It was a tight little
European thriller.

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:08.234
But I still thought it would go
straight to video.

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:09.467
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.467 --> 00:06:11.567
And it went on to make like over
a billion dollars.

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:14.000
So congrats. I want to talk
about "Blacklight."

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.934
More with Liam Neeson
when we come back.

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:16.968
Stick around, everybody.

